Temporary-file registry checks
==============================

  ./maxima-local --no-init --lisp=sbcl \
    --batch-string='run_testsuite(tests=[rtest_plotoptions]);'

Run every configured Lisp and the complete core+share suite. Fourteen
appended examples retain previous problem numbers and expected results.
Require the full test count and inspect errors even when Maxima exits zero.

PLOT-TEMP-FILE0 protects registration with a short portable lock.
REGISTERED-TEMP-FILES copies the registered keys under the same lock.
DELETE-TEMP-FILES processes that snapshot outside the lock, retaining the
registry and its existing handling of directories, absent files and probe
errors. A filename registered during cleanup is eligible on the next call.
Filename formatting, preserve flags and the random naming algorithm retain
their existing behavior. These helpers do not provide atomic file creation.

Tests replace the actual shared registry only in an otherwise idle test
process and restore it after workers join. They cover 63 path/preserve
combinations, equal duplicate keys, an independent snapshot list, 4,096
unique registrations, concurrent prefix-consistent snapshots, and native
and one-runner fallback execution. Four readers each take 16 snapshots.

Cleanup tests create their own files with :IF-EXISTS :ERROR and remove them
on exit. They check missing/malformed keys, preserved files and a worker
registering a later file during cleanup. A custom pathname printer verifies
that user Lisp callbacks and errors occur outside the lock. Tests neither
render plots nor launch Gnuplot.

Ordinary locking does not make arbitrary external accesses to the hash safe,
coordinate concurrent process shutdown, or certify asynchronous worker
termination. Gnuplot pipe state and draw options require separate work.
